Switch: the deko3d NRO keeps Dawn's blob cache in a file of its own (AURORA_GFX_DEKO3D)

The deko3d NRO shares native/user/cache/ with the GL NRO (the pipeline list cache, pipeline_cache.db,
is the same on purpose), but Dawn's blob cache, dawn_cache.db, holds the GL NRO's program binaries,
and cache_prune deletes the rows a session did not use: one run of the deko3d NRO (Dawn's Null
device, other keys) emptied it, and the GL NRO's next start rebuilt every program behind a ~2.5 min
"Preparing shaders" screen (console, 2026-10-08). With AURORA_GFX_DEKO3D the file is
dawn_cache_dk.db. Without it (the GL NRO, the Mac) nothing changes.

Switch only (switch/native/aurora/patches); not for upstream.

diff --git a/lib/webgpu/gpu_cache.cpp b/lib/webgpu/gpu_cache.cpp
index 8ba35f6..6bafb95 100644
--- a/lib/webgpu/gpu_cache.cpp
+++ b/lib/webgpu/gpu_cache.cpp
@@ -39,7 +39,12 @@ constexpr int CACHE_SCHEMA = 2;
 constexpr uint64_t VacuumPrunePercentThreshold = 25;
 
 static std::filesystem::path cache_path() {
+#if defined(AURORA_GFX_DEKO3D)
+  // the GL NRO's file would be pruned to this NRO's keys
+  return io::fs_path_from_string(g_config.cachePath) / "dawn_cache_dk.db";
+#else
   return io::fs_path_from_string(g_config.cachePath) / "dawn_cache.db";
+#endif
 }
 
